## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to reason with Kleene's three-valued logic and implement a lightweight backtracking propagator over a small, non-binary constraint set.

## Key Concepts
- **Kleene 3-valued semantics**: Values ordered T > U > F; negation of U remains U
- **Implication equivalence**: a→b = ¬a ∨ b
- **Constraint propagation**: Propagating partial information through implications
- **Goal**: Produce a non-F assignment that still utilizes the unknown value U

## Code Example
```javascript
function not(v) {
  if (v === 'T') return 'F';
  if (v === 'F') return 'T';
  return 'U';
}

function or(a, b) {
  if (a === 'T' || b === 'T') return 'T';
  if (a === 'F' && b === 'F') return 'F';
  return 'U';
}

function and(a, b) {
  if (a === 'F' || b === 'F') return 'F';
  if (a === 'T' && b === 'T') return 'T';
  return 'U';
}

function evalRule(rule, vars) {
  const [a, b] = rule.map(v => vars[v]);
  return or(not(a), b);
}

function propagate(vars, rules) {
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const result = evalRule(rule, vars);
    if (result === 'F') return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
